course: dictionary
lesson: 7976
title: Recollection: memories and remembering
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A recollection is a memory of something from the past. In «then back come the recollections one by one, like homing pigeons», the memories are coming back to the mind, one after another, like birds flying home.
explain: Recollection can also mean the ability to remember. «I have no recollection of it» means you cannot remember it at all. The word «no» is the clue: the memory is simply not there.
explain: People often say «to the best of my recollection» when they want to show they are not completely sure. It means «as far as I can remember». Recollection comes from the verb recollect, which means to remember.
fact: Recollection means a memory of something from the past.
fact: «Recollect» is the verb: to remember something.
fact: «I have no recollection of it» means you cannot remember it at all.
fact: «To the best of my recollection» means as far as I can remember.
fact: In church, a recollection is a calm, quiet prayer and thoughtfulness.
exercise: «Then back come the recollections one by one, like homing pigeons.» What does recollections mean here? | *Memories of the past coming back | Loud shouts in a playground | Lost keys and missing socks | Birds flying over the sea
exercise: Maya says, «I have no recollection of it.» What does she mean? | She is writing a letter about it | She has lost her bag | *She cannot remember it at all | She remembers it very clearly
exercise: Grandad says, «To the best of my recollection, the bus left at nine.» What does the phrase show? | He heard it from a friend | *He is saying it is as far as he can remember | The bus was late that day | He has checked the timetable and is certain
test:
A «vague recollection» means | *A memory that is not very clear | A very loud and clear sound | A happy memory of a holiday | A brand new idea
Which word is the verb meaning to remember? | *recollect | collect | collection | election
exam:
In church, a recollection is a calm, quiet prayer and thoughtfulness. Which word is the best meaning here? | *Calm, quiet prayer and thoughtfulness | A memory of a holiday by the sea | The ability to remember a phone number | A loud song sung by a choir
